— cosmetic only; the one thing to watch is the spinner hiding under the transparent status bar on API 35+.\n\nTASK-5: Manually verify on a device/emulator (Android <15 and 15+, light and dark): pull at top reloads; scrolling a long list back up does not; no trigger inside modals/bottom sheets, kanban drag or calendar drag; share-intent still works; record the results in implementation.md. Add a short changelog line for the next F-Droid version if the release process expects it.\n  files: docs/jobs/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload/implementation.md, fastlane/metadata/android/en-US/changelogs/<next versionCode>.txt (only if wanted)\n  depends: TASK-3, TASK-4\n  risk: low — verification only. The repo has no automated UI tests, so this is the only check of the gesture behaviour.\n\n## Out of scope (by this plan)\n\n- Any change in `frontend/` (vendored; it would be overwritten). A web-based or\n  PWA pull-to-refresh would belong in the `app` repo as a separate job.\n- Soft data re-fetch without a full reload.\n- Version bump / release (`scripts/release.sh`).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":17,"newStart":1,"newLines":85,"lines":[" # Tasks: Swipe from top to reload"," "," id: object","-analyst:","-date:","+analyst: @analyst","+date: 2026-10-14"," ","-<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->","+## Context (what the analyst found)"," ","+- Branch verified: worktree HEAD is `feature/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload`, matching `brief.md`.","+- This repo (`mobile`) is a Capacitor 7 Android shell. `frontend/` is **vendored**","+  from the canonical app repo (`../app`) by `scripts/vendor.sh` (`rsync --delete`),","+  with mobile-only overrides kept in `patch/`. Any edit made directly in","+  `frontend/src` will be **wiped on the next vendor/release run**, so","+  this job must not change `frontend/`.","+- Because of that, the plan is a **native Android** pull-to-refresh: wrap the","+  Capacitor WebView in AndroidX `SwipeRefreshLayout`, which gives the standard","+  Material circular spinner that Android users expect. Everything stays in","+  `android/`.","+- **Key pitfall:** the web app never scrolls the document itself. In","+  `frontend/src/routes/+layout.svelte` the root `.page-container` is","+  `overflow-hidden` and the content scrolls inside","+  `<div class=\"... overflow-auto content-container\">`, and there are other nested","+  scrollers too (modals, kanban, calendar views). So `WebView.getScrollY()` /","+  `canScrollVertically(-1)` will always say \"at top\", and a plain","+  `SwipeRefreshLayout` would start a refresh whenever the user scrolls a list","+  back up. The native side has to ask the page whether the element under the","+  finger is scrolled to the top (TASK-3).","+- Capacitor's `BridgeActivity` sets its own content layout","+  (`capacitor_bridge_layout_main`); `android/app/src/main/res/layout/activity_main.xml`","+  looks unused. So wrapping should probably happen in code in `MainActivity`","+  (re-parent the bridge WebView), not in XML. The developer should check this","+  against the installed `@capacitor/android` sources before starting TASK-2.","+","+## Open questions / assumptions (not blocking; flag if wrong)","+","+1. **New Gradle dependency.** `androidx.swiperefreshlayout:swiperefreshlayout`","+   is not on the classpath yet. It is a standard AndroidX library from Google","+   Maven, which F-Droid builds accept. Project rules say \"never install packages","+   without asking\". That rule is written for npm, but the developer/reviewer","+   should get explicit sign-off on this addition.","+2. **What \"reload\" means.** Assumption: a full `WebView.reload()` of the current","+   route. It is simple and also fixes \"didn't load properly\" cases. Side effect:","+   in-memory UI state is lost (e.g. an unsaved note in the editor or an open","+   modal). A softer \"re-fetch data only\" option would need changes in the","+   vendored frontend and is out of scope here.","+3. **Where the gesture is disabled.** Assumption: no refresh when the touch","+   starts inside a scrolled element, inside an open modal/dialog or bottom","+   sheet, or during a drag (kanban dnd, calendar entry drag). Exact rules are","+   settled in TASK-3.","+4. Spinner colours: assumption is to reuse the existing","+   `solyto_bg_light/dark` colours plus a contrasting accent. No new design input.","+"," ## Task breakdown"," ","-<!-- TASK-1: description","-     files: list of files likely affected","-     depends: none","-     risk: low / medium / high — reason","+TASK-1: Add the AndroidX SwipeRefreshLayout dependency (version pinned in `variables.gradle`) and confirm the project still builds.","+  files: android/variables.gradle, android/app/build.gradle","+  depends: none (needs dependency sign-off, see open question 1)","+  risk: low — a single well-known AndroidX artifact, but it must resolve in the F-Droid build environment (`scripts/build-fdroid.sh`)."," ","-TASK-2: ...","--->","+TASK-2: In `MainActivity`, wrap the Capacitor bridge WebView in a `SwipeRefreshLayout` in code (keep its layout params and edge-to-edge inset handling), and on refresh call `webView.reload()` and stop the spinner when the page finishes loading.","+  files: android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/MainActivity.java","+  depends: TASK-1","+  risk: medium — re-parenting the bridge WebView after `super.onCreate` could interfere with Capacitor's `adjustMarginsForEdgeToEdge: \"auto\"` insets and with the share-intent `loadUrl`. Finishing the refresh needs a page-load hook that doesn't replace Capacitor's own `WebViewClient` (e.g. a `BridgeWebViewClient` subclass / `WebViewListener`, or a timeout fallback).","+","+TASK-3: Gate the gesture with `setOnChildScrollUpCallback`, backed by a small script that the native side injects into the WebView (no `frontend/` edits). On touchstart, the script finds the nearest scrollable ancestor of the touch target and reports to native (JavascriptInterface or a cached flag) whether it can scroll up, or whether the touch is inside an open modal/dialog. Refresh is allowed only when nothing under the finger can scroll up.","+  files: android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/MainActivity.java (possibly a small new helper class in the same package)","+  depends: TASK-2","+  risk: high — this decides whether the feature feels right or keeps firing by accident. Without it, scrolling up in any list triggers a reload (see Context). It also has a timing race (touchstart in JS vs. native intercept), and the script has to be re-injected after each page load/reload.","+","+TASK-4: Style the indicator: spinner/background colours that follow light/dark mode (reusing the existing `solyto_bg_*` colours), and a start offset so it shows below the status bar under edge-to-edge on Android 15+.","+  files: android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/MainActivity.java, android/app/src/main/res/values/colors.xml","+  depends: TASK-2","+  risk: low — cosmetic only; the one thing to watch is the spinner hiding under the transparent status bar on API 35+.","+","+TASK-5: Manually verify on a device/emulator (Android <15 and 15+, light and dark): pull at top reloads; scrolling a long list back up does not; no trigger inside modals/bottom sheets, kanban drag or calendar drag; share-intent still works; record the results in implementation.md. Add a short changelog line for the next F-Droid version if the release process expects it.","+  files: docs/jobs/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload/implementation.md, fastlane/metadata/android/en-US/changelogs/<next versionCode>.txt (only if wanted)","+  depends: TASK-3, TASK-4","+  risk: low — verification only. The repo has no automated UI tests, so this is the only check of the gesture behaviour.","+","+## Out of scope (by this plan)","+","+- Any change in `frontend/` (vendored; it would be overwritten). A web-based or","+  PWA pull-to-refresh would belong in the `app` repo as a separate job.","+- Soft data re-fetch without a full reload.","+- Version bump / release (`scripts/release.sh`)."]}],"originalFile":"# Tasks: Swipe from top to reload\n\nid: object\nanalyst:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n<!-- TASK-1: description\n     files: list of files likely affected\n     depends: none\n     risk: low / medium / high — reason\n\nTASK-2: ...\n-->\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0185353wS8FpBTWDdna44Fbn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
