t` subclass that handles the\n  timing race. `ACTION_DOWN` is always let through, so the layout records the\n  start point. Move events then stay blocked until the page answers for that\n  touch, or until 300 ms pass, after which a pull is allowed.\n\nI checked the injected script with `node --check`, and ran it in headless\nChromium against a fixture page with a mocked bridge. Results: plain element at\ntop → allowed; inside a scrolled list → blocked; fixed modal → blocked;\n`touch-action:none` → blocked; `touch-action:pan-y` → allowed;\n`preventDefault` on touchmove → blocked mid-gesture; a second injection only\nre-reports ready.\n\nTASK-4: Spinner colours follow the system light/dark mode and are re-applied\nin `onConfigurationChanged` (the manifest handles `uiMode` itself). The circle\nbackground is `solyto_bg_light` (#FFFFFF) in light mode and the new\n`solyto_surface_dark` (#222222, the web app's `s-dark-2`) in dark mode. The\narrow cycles through the app's gradient colours, `solyto_lightblue` #14A5CD and\n`solyto_green` #61D96A (new entries in `colors.xml`). The spinner position is\ntied to the WebView's top: a layout listener calls `setProgressViewOffset`, so\non Android 15+ edge-to-edge the spinner rests 64 dp below the status bar\ninstead of under it. Below Android 15 the top is 0 and SwipeRefreshLayout's\ndefaults are kept.\n\nTASK-5: **Not done.** No device verification was possible: this environment\nhas no Java toolchain, Android SDK or emulator, so I could neither build the\nAPK nor run it. Only the parts that run in a browser were checked (TASK-3,\nabove). Checklist still to run on a device/emulator (Android 14 and 15+, light\nand dark):\n- [ ] project builds (`./gradlew assembleDebug`) and the dependency resolves\n      in the F-Droid build\n- [ ] pull at the top of a page shows the spinner and reloads\n- [ ] scrolling a long list back up does not reload\n- [ ] no reload inside a modal/bottom sheet, kanban drag or calendar drag\n- [ ] spinner appears below the status bar on Android 15+ and the WebView\n      still has correct edge-to-edge margins\n- [ ] share intent (\"Share → solyto\") still opens `/share`\n\nNo changelog line was added: `fastlane/.../changelogs/` only has `10012.txt`,\nso the release process doesn't seem to expect one per version.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- The code has not been compiled or tested on a device (see TASK-5). This must\n  be done before release.\n- A reload is a full `WebView.reload()`, so unsaved in-memory UI state (e.g. an\n  open editor or modal) is lost. A softer data-only refresh would need\n  frontend changes in the `app` repo.\n- Spinner colours follow the system dark mode, the same as the existing\n  system-bar code, not the web app's own theme setting (`html.dark`).\n- On Android 15+ the spinner starts just above the WebView top, i.e. behind\n  the transparent status bar, while it is being pulled in. This is\n  cosmetic; please check on a device.\n- `MainActivity` already called `handleShareIntent` twice on cold start\n  (`BridgeActivity.load()` calls `onNewIntent`, then `onCreate` calls it\n  again). This is unchanged and out of scope.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":19,"newStart":1,"newLines":116,"lines":[" # Implementation: Swipe from top to reload"," "," id: object","-developer:","-date:","+developer: @developer","+date: 2026-10-14"," ","-<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->","-"," ## Summary"," ","-<!-- What was implemented, task by task. Reference task IDs. -->","+Native Android pull-to-refresh, done entirely in `android/` (no changes to the","+vendored `frontend/`). The Capacitor WebView is wrapped in an AndroidX","+`SwipeRefreshLayout`, so pulling down shows the standard Material spinner and","+runs `WebView.reload()`. A small script injected into the page decides","+whether a pull may start, based on what is under the finger. This stops a","+reload when the user scrolls a list back up, and inside modals, fixed sheets","+and drag/gesture areas."," ","+**Not built and not tested on a device.** This environment has no JDK, no","+Android SDK and no emulator, so the Java code has not been compiled. See","+TASK-5 below.","+"," ## Changes"," ","-<!-- List of files changed and what changed in each. -->","+TASK-1: Added `androidx.swiperefreshlayout:swiperefreshlayout:1.1.0` (version","+pinned as `androidxSwipeRefreshLayoutVersion` in `android/variables.gradle`,","+used in `android/app/build.gradle`). The brief allows new dependencies, which","+answers open question 1. The artifact is on Google Maven, which F-Droid already","+uses for the other AndroidX libraries. I read its sources to confirm the API","+(`setOnChildScrollUpCallback`, `setProgressViewOffset`,","+`getProgressCircleDiameter`, and the intercept logic)."," ","+TASK-2: `MainActivity.setupPullToRefresh()` re-parents the bridge WebView after","+`super.onCreate`, giving CoordinatorLayout → SwipeRefreshLayout → FrameLayout","+→ WebView. I checked this against the `@capacitor/android` 7.6.8 sources:","+`BridgeActivity` uses `capacitor_bridge_layout_main`, and","+`CapacitorWebView.edgeToEdgeHandler` insets the WebView by setting its own","+layout margins. `SwipeRefreshLayout` ignores child margins, so the extra","+FrameLayout is needed to keep Capacitor's edge-to-edge handling working. The","+existing margins are copied over and insets are re-requested. On refresh,","+`webView.reload()` is called. The spinner stops through a","+`Bridge.addWebViewListener` (`onPageLoaded` / `onReceivedError`), which leaves","+Capacitor's own WebViewClient untouched, plus a 15 s timeout as a fallback.","+The share-intent `loadUrl` is unchanged.","+","+TASK-3: Two new classes in `app.solyto`:","+- `PullToRefreshPlugin`: a Capacitor plugin with no methods, registered in","+  `MainActivity.onCreate` before `super.onCreate`. I made it a plugin so that","+  `addJavascriptInterface` runs during bridge setup, before the first page","+  loads (interfaces added later only appear after the next reload). After each","+  page load it injects a script (guarded so it installs only once per page).","+  On `touchstart` the script reports \"blocked\" if any of these is true:","+  - more than one finger is down, or the page is pinch-zoomed","+  - the document or any ancestor of the target has `scrollTop > 0`","+  - the target is inside `dialog[open]`, `[role=dialog|alertdialog]`,","+    `[aria-modal=true]` or any `position: fixed` element (this covers","+    `PopupContentModal`, the mobile nav overlays and the FAB)","+  - an ancestor has a `touch-action` that excludes vertical panning (e.g. maps)","+","+  If a page handler calls `preventDefault()` on `touchmove`, as","+  svelte-dnd-action does once a drag starts, the script also reports blocked","+  mid-gesture. If a page has no script (still loading, or an error page), the","+  check falls back to `webView.canScrollVertically(-1)`.","+- `PullToRefreshLayout`: a `SwipeRefreshLayout` subclass that handles the","+  timing race. `ACTION_DOWN` is always let through, so the layout records the","+  start point. Move events then stay blocked until the page answers for that","+  touch, or until 300 ms pass, after which a pull is allowed.","+","+I checked the injected script with `node --check`, and ran it in headless","+Chromium against a fixture page with a mocked bridge. Results: plain element at","+top → allowed; inside a scrolled list → blocked; fixed modal → blocked;","+`touch-action:none` → blocked; `touch-action:pan-y` → allowed;","+`preventDefault` on touchmove → blocked mid-gesture; a second injection only","+re-reports ready.","+","+TASK-4: Spinner colours follow the system light/dark mode and are re-applied","+in `onConfigurationChanged` (the manifest handles `uiMode` itself). The circle","+background is `solyto_bg_light` (#FFFFFF) in light mode and the new","+`solyto_surface_dark` (#222222, the web app's `s-dark-2`) in dark mode. The","+arrow cycles through the app's gradient colours, `solyto_lightblue` #14A5CD and","+`solyto_green` #61D96A (new entries in `colors.xml`). The spinner position is","+tied to the WebView's top: a layout listener calls `setProgressViewOffset`, so","+on Android 15+ edge-to-edge the spinner rests 64 dp below the status bar","+instead of under it. Below Android 15 the top is 0 and SwipeRefreshLayout's","+defaults are kept.","+","+TASK-5: **Not done.** No device verification was possible: this environment","+has no Java toolchain, Android SDK or emulator, so I could neither build the","+APK nor run it. Only the parts that run in a browser were checked (TASK-3,","+above). Checklist still to run on a device/emulator (Android 14 and 15+, light","+and dark):","+- [ ] project builds (`./gradlew assembleDebug`) and the dependency resolves","+      in the F-Droid build","+- [ ] pull at the top of a page shows the spinner and reloads","+- [ ] scrolling a long list back up does not reload","+- [ ] no reload inside a modal/bottom sheet, kanban drag or calendar drag","+- [ ] spinner appears below the status bar on Android 15+ and the WebView","+      still has correct edge-to-edge margins","+- [ ] share intent (\"Share → solyto\") still opens `/share`","+","+No changelog line was added: `fastlane/.../changelogs/` only has `10012.txt`,","+so the release process doesn't seem to expect one per version.","+"," ## Known issues / follow-ups"," ","-<!-- Anything that came up during implementation that wasn't in scope but should be tracked. -->","+- The code has not been compiled or tested on a device (see TASK-5). This must","+  be done before release.","+- A reload is a full `WebView.reload()`, so unsaved in-memory UI state (e.g. an","+  open editor or modal) is lost. A softer data-only refresh would need","+  frontend changes in the `app` repo.","+- Spinner colours follow the system dark mode, the same as the existing","+  system-bar code, not the web app's own theme setting (`html.dark`).","+- On Android 15+ the spinner starts just above the WebView top, i.e. behind","+  the transparent status bar, while it is being pulled in. This is","+  cosmetic; please check on a device.","+- `MainActivity` already called `handleShareIntent` twice on cold start","+  (`BridgeActivity.load()` calls `onNewIntent`, then `onCreate` calls it","+  again). This is unchanged and out of scope."]}],"originalFile":"# Implementation: Swipe from top to reload\n\nid: object\ndeveloper:\ndate:\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\n<!-- What was implemented, task by task. Reference task IDs. -->\n\n## Changes\n\n<!-- List of files changed and what changed in each. -->\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n<!-- Anything that came up during implementation that wasn't in scope but should be tracked. -->\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Dn2oTd6AYjtki4epVQEKr9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
