{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg2K6ShukJJmU152URtpi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pull-to-refresh is now in the Android app on `feature/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload`, but none of it has been compiled or run on a device. This environment has no JDK, no Android SDK and no emulator, so a device check is still needed before release.\n\n**What it does**\n- Pulling down at the top of the app shows the standard Android round spinner and reloads the page. The spinner stops when the page finishes loading, or after 15 seconds at most.\n- All changes are in `android/`. Nothing in `frontend/` changed, since that folder is overwritten each time the app is vendored.\n- **New dependency:** AndroidX `swiperefreshlayout` 1.1.0, from Google's Maven repository. The brief allowed new dependencies.\n\n**When a pull does not reload**\nThe web app scrolls inside nested elements, so Android always thinks the page is \"at the top\". Without extra handling, scrolling any list back up would reload the page. To prevent that, a small script is added to each page; on every touch it tells the native side whether a pull is allowed. A pull does nothing when:\n- a list or editor under the finger is scrolled down,\n- the touch is inside a modal, dialog or anything fixed on screen (popups, mobile nav overlays, the add button),\n- the area handles its own touch gestures (for example maps),\n- a drag has started (kanban, reordering),\n- two fingers are down or the page is zoomed in.\n\n**Look**\n- The spinner circle is white in light mode and dark grey (#222222) in dark mode, following the system setting.\n- The arrow cycles through the app's light blue and green.\n- On Android 15+ the spinner settles below the status bar.\n\n**What I could check**\nI ran the touch-check script in headless Chromium against a test page with a fake native side. Every case behaved as intended: a plain area allows the pull; a scrolled list, a modal, a `touch-action:none` area and a drag all block it. I also checked the Capacitor 7.6.8 and SwipeRefreshLayout source code to confirm the parts I rely on.\n\n**Still to do**\n`implementation.md` has a checklist:\n- build the project and confirm the F-Droid build pulls in the new dependency,\n- pull at the top on Android 14 and 15+, in light and dark mode,\n- scroll a list back up and confirm it doesn't reload,\n- try modals, kanban drag and calendar drag,\n- confirm sharing text into the app still works.\n\n**Worth knowing**\n- A pull reloads the whole page, so anything unsaved in an open editor or modal is lost.\n- Spinner colours follow the system dark mode, not the app's own theme setting.\n- I didn't add a changelog file, because the changelogs folder only has one for version 10012.\n\nThe worktree is clean, with one commit per task plus the summary."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":71776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":293},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d54107cb-0f69-469c-bea7-76a86cb5f7dc","uuid":"4801702d-9179-4740-8c43-1a465ac24a6e","timestamp":"2026-10-14T14:47:55.579Z","request_id":"req_011Cg2K6SLLPj7oDGrrPxWff"}
