{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg2KCwtWZDLjQLTPweRos","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YU14K2gZDeFstsg8qhcwMq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload/verdict.md","content":"# Verdict: Swipe from top to reload\n\nid: object\nreviewer: @reviewer\ndate: 2026-10-14\n\n## Review\n\nBranch checked: `feature/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload` (matches brief).\nBase: `main` (`.manigot/manigot.json` is missing, so I used the default).\nI reviewed the whole `git diff main...HEAD`. Every source change is in `android/`;\n`frontend/` was not touched, as the plan required.\n\nI could not compile anything either: there is no JDK, Gradle, Android SDK or\n`node_modules/@capacitor` here. So the Java was checked by reading only, against\nthe Capacitor 7.6.8 sources the developer quoted in `session.log`\n(`CapacitorWebView.edgeToEdgeHandler`, `WebViewListener`, `BridgeActivity`).\n\nTASK-1: PARTIAL\nnotes: `android/variables.gradle` pins `androidxSwipeRefreshLayoutVersion = '1.1.0'`\nand `android/app/build.gradle` uses it. That part is correct, and the brief\nallows new dependencies. The task also says \"confirm the project still builds\",\nand that was not done: the dependency has never been resolved and the new code\nhas never been compiled.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `MainActivity.setupPullToRefresh()` re-parents the WebView as\nSwipeRefreshLayout → FrameLayout → WebView. The FrameLayout is needed:\nCapacitor's edge-to-edge listener writes `MarginLayoutParams` on the WebView\nitself, and `SwipeRefreshLayout` ignores child margins. The existing margins\nare copied into `FrameLayout.LayoutParams`, and insets are re-requested. The\nspinner stops through `Bridge.addWebViewListener` (`onPageLoaded` /\n`onReceivedError`), so Capacitor's own WebViewClient is left alone. There is\nalso a 15 s timeout as a fallback. The share-intent code is unchanged.\n\nTASK-3: PASS\nnotes: The plugin is registered before `super.onCreate`, so `load()` adds the\nJS interface before `loadWebView()`. The ready flag is reset in\n`onPageStarted`, and the script is re-injected in `onPageLoaded`.\n`PullToRefreshLayout` always lets `ACTION_DOWN` through so the start Y is\nrecorded, then blocks move events until the page answers or 300 ms pass. This\nfits SwipeRefreshLayout 1.1.0's intercept logic. The blocking rules are\nreasonable for this frontend. The root `.page-container` /\n`.content-container` are not `position: fixed`, so a normal pull still works.\nThe calendar views' `touch-action: pan-y` is allowed. The JS interface only\nexposes `ready()` and `report(boolean)`, so there is no meaningful attack\nsurface. Release builds use `minifyEnabled false`, so ProGuard won't strip it.\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: The light/dark colours are re-applied in `onConfigurationChanged`. The\nnew colours are added to `colors.xml`. `setProgressViewOffset` is tied to\n`webView.getTop()`, and it is never called while a refresh is running.\n\nTASK-5: FAIL\nnotes: Not done (the developer says so openly in `implementation.md`). No\nbuild, no emulator/device run. The repo has no automated UI tests, so nothing\nelse checks the gesture behaviour. Leaving out the changelog is justified\n(only `10012.txt` exists).\n\nScope: `docs/CLAUDE.md` (an empty file) was added in a `chore: commit all`\ncommit and is not mentioned in `implementation.md`. It looks like tooling, not\ndeveloper work, so it is not a blocker. Nothing else is outside the plan.\n\n## Security\n\nNot run separately. Reviewer note: the added JavascriptInterface only takes\nbooleans. It does nothing else and has no side effects beyond gating the\ngesture.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nThe code reads correctly and matches the plan. But it has never been compiled\nor run, and the plan makes both of these acceptance criteria (TASK-1 \"confirm\nthe project still builds\", TASK-5). Someone with an Android toolchain must do\nthe following before merge:\n\n1. Run `./gradlew assembleDebug` (and the F-Droid build, `scripts/build-fdroid.sh`)\n   and confirm that `androidx.swiperefreshlayout:swiperefreshlayout:1.1.0`\n   resolves and the three Java files compile.\n2. Work through the TASK-5 checklist in `implementation.md` on Android <15\n   and 15+, in light and dark mode:\n   - pulling at the top reloads\n   - scrolling a long list back up does not reload\n   - no reload inside a modal, bottom sheet, kanban drag or calendar drag\n   - the spinner shows below the status bar and the WebView's edge-to-edge\n     margins are still correct\n   - the share intent still opens `/share`\n\n   Record the results in `implementation.md`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1265,"cache_read_input_tokens":27753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1265},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0df14cb-790b-4cc9-af4f-67f3c4d6310e","uuid":"a5519393-b7b1-47e6-a323-188c184d7de5","timestamp":"2026-10-14T14:49:33.453Z","request_id":"req_011Cg2KCwXS2RjG7nZWdTCsK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YU14K2gZDeFstsg8qhcwMq":{"file_path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload/verdict.md","content":"# Verdict: Swipe from top to reload\n\nid: object\nreviewer: @reviewer\ndate: 2026-10-14\n\n## Review\n\nBranch checked: `feature/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload` (matches brief).\nBase: `main` (`.manigot/manigot.json` is missing, so I used the default).\nI reviewed the whole `git diff main...HEAD`. Every source change is in `android/`;\n`frontend/` was not touched, as the plan required.\n\nI could not compile anything either: there is no JDK, Gradle, Android SDK or\n`node_modules/@capacitor` here. So the Java was checked by reading only, against\nthe Capacitor 7.6.8 sources the developer quoted in `session.log`\n(`CapacitorWebView.edgeToEdgeHandler`, `WebViewListener`, `BridgeActivity`).\n\nTASK-1: PARTIAL\nnotes: `android/variables.gradle` pins `androidxSwipeRefreshLayoutVersion = '1.1.0'`\nand `android/app/build.gradle` uses it. That part is correct, and the brief\nallows new dependencies. The task also says \"confirm the project still builds\",\nand that was not done: the dependency has never been resolved and the new code\nhas never been compiled.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `MainActivity.setupPullToRefresh()` re-parents the WebView as\nSwipeRefreshLayout → FrameLayout → WebView. The FrameLayout is needed:\nCapacitor's edge-to-edge listener writes `MarginLayoutParams` on the WebView\nitself, and `SwipeRefreshLayout` ignores child margins. The existing margins\nare copied into `FrameLayout.LayoutParams`, and insets are re-requested. The\nspinner stops through `Bridge.addWebViewListener` (`onPageLoaded` /\n`onReceivedError`), so Capacitor's own WebViewClient is left alone. There is\nalso a 15 s timeout as a fallback. The share-intent code is unchanged.\n\nTASK-3: PASS\nnotes: The plugin is registered before `super.onCreate`, so `load()` adds the\nJS interface before `loadWebView()`. The ready flag is reset in\n`onPageStarted`, and the script is re-injected in `onPageLoaded`.\n`PullToRefreshLayout` always lets `ACTION_DOWN` through so the start Y is\nrecorded, then blocks move events until the page answers or 300 ms pass. This\nfits SwipeRefreshLayout 1.1.0's intercept logic. The blocking rules are\nreasonable for this frontend. The root `.page-container` /\n`.content-container` are not `position: fixed`, so a normal pull still works.\nThe calendar views' `touch-action: pan-y` is allowed. The JS interface only\nexposes `ready()` and `report(boolean)`, so there is no meaningful attack\nsurface. Release builds use `minifyEnabled false`, so ProGuard won't strip it.\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: The light/dark colours are re-applied in `onConfigurationChanged`. The\nnew colours are added to `colors.xml`. `setProgressViewOffset` is tied to\n`webView.getTop()`, and it is never called while a refresh is running.\n\nTASK-5: FAIL\nnotes: Not done (the developer says so openly in `implementation.md`). No\nbuild, no emulator/device run. The repo has no automated UI tests, so nothing\nelse checks the gesture behaviour. Leaving out the changelog is justified\n(only `10012.txt` exists).\n\nScope: `docs/CLAUDE.md` (an empty file) was added in a `chore: commit all`\ncommit and is not mentioned in `implementation.md`. It looks like tooling, not\ndeveloper work, so it is not a blocker. Nothing else is outside the plan.\n\n## Security\n\nNot run separately. Reviewer note: the added JavascriptInterface only takes\nbooleans. It does nothing else and has no side effects beyond gating the\ngesture.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nThe code reads correctly and matches the plan. But it has never been compiled\nor run, and the plan makes both of these acceptance criteria (TASK-1 \"confirm\nthe project still builds\", TASK-5). Someone with an Android toolchain must do\nthe following before merge:\n\n1. Run `./gradlew assembleDebug` (and the F-Droid build, `scripts/build-fdroid.sh`)\n   and confirm that `androidx.swiperefreshlayout:swiperefreshlayout:1.1.0`\n   resolves and the three Java files compile.\n2. Work through the TASK-5 checklist in `implementation.md` on Android <15\n   and 15+, in light and dark mode:\n   - pulling at the top reloads\n   - scrolling a long list back up does not reload\n   - no reload inside a modal, bottom sheet, kanban drag or calendar drag\n   - the spinner shows below the status bar and the WebView's edge-to-edge\n     margins are still correct\n   - the share intent still opens `/share`\n\n   Record the results in `implementation.md`.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YU14K2gZDeFstsg8qhcwMq","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/docs/jobs/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload/verdict.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0df14cb-790b-4cc9-af4f-67f3c4d6310e","uuid":"0c2aac74-6722-4e46-8375-e58744b27c42","timestamp":"2026-10-14T14:49:33.498Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload/verdict.md","content":"# Verdict: Swipe from top to reload\n\nid: object\nreviewer: @reviewer\ndate: 2026-10-14\n\n## Review\n\nBranch checked: `feature/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload` (matches brief).\nBase: `main` (`.manigot/manigot.json` is missing, so I used the default).\nI reviewed the whole `git diff main...HEAD`. Every source change is in `android/`;\n`frontend/` was not touched, as the plan required.\n\nI could not compile anything either: there is no JDK, Gradle, Android SDK or\n`node_modules/@capacitor` here. So the Java was checked by reading only, against\nthe Capacitor 7.6.8 sources the developer quoted in `session.log`\n(`CapacitorWebView.edgeToEdgeHandler`, `WebViewListener`, `BridgeActivity`).\n\nTASK-1: PARTIAL\nnotes: `android/variables.gradle` pins `androidxSwipeRefreshLayoutVersion = '1.1.0'`\nand `android/app/build.gradle` uses it. That part is correct, and the brief\nallows new dependencies. The task also says \"confirm the project still builds\",\nand that was not done: the dependency has never been resolved and the new code\nhas never been compiled.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `MainActivity.setupPullToRefresh()` re-parents the WebView as\nSwipeRefreshLayout → FrameLayout → WebView. The FrameLayout is needed:\nCapacitor's edge-to-edge listener writes `MarginLayoutParams` on the WebView\nitself, and `SwipeRefreshLayout` ignores child margins. The existing margins\nare copied into `FrameLayout.LayoutParams`, and insets are re-requested. The\nspinner stops through `Bridge.addWebViewListener` (`onPageLoaded` /\n`onReceivedError`), so Capacitor's own WebViewClient is left alone. There is\nalso a 15 s timeout as a fallback. The share-intent code is unchanged.\n\nTASK-3: PASS\nnotes: The plugin is registered before `super.onCreate`, so `load()` adds the\nJS interface before `loadWebView()`. The ready flag is reset in\n`onPageStarted`, and the script is re-injected in `onPageLoaded`.\n`PullToRefreshLayout` always lets `ACTION_DOWN` through so the start Y is\nrecorded, then blocks move events until the page answers or 300 ms pass. This\nfits SwipeRefreshLayout 1.1.0's intercept logic. The blocking rules are\nreasonable for this frontend. The root `.page-container` /\n`.content-container` are not `position: fixed`, so a normal pull still works.\nThe calendar views' `touch-action: pan-y` is allowed. The JS interface only\nexposes `ready()` and `report(boolean)`, so there is no meaningful attack\nsurface. Release builds use `minifyEnabled false`, so ProGuard won't strip it.\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: The light/dark colours are re-applied in `onConfigurationChanged`. The\nnew colours are added to `colors.xml`. `setProgressViewOffset` is tied to\n`webView.getTop()`, and it is never called while a refresh is running.\n\nTASK-5: FAIL\nnotes: Not done (the developer says so openly in `implementation.md`). No\nbuild, no emulator/device run. The repo has no automated UI tests, so nothing\nelse checks the gesture behaviour. Leaving out the changelog is justified\n(only `10012.txt` exists).\n\nScope: `docs/CLAUDE.md` (an empty file) was added in a `chore: commit all`\ncommit and is not mentioned in `implementation.md`. It looks like tooling, not\ndeveloper work, so it is not a blocker. Nothing else is outside the plan.\n\n## Security\n\nNot run separately. Reviewer note: the added JavascriptInterface only takes\nbooleans. It does nothing else and has no side effects beyond gating the\ngesture.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nThe code reads correctly and matches the plan. But it has never been compiled\nor run, and the plan makes both of these acceptance criteria (TASK-1 \"confirm\nthe project still builds\", TASK-5). Someone with an Android toolchain must do\nthe following before merge:\n\n1. Run `./gradlew assembleDebug` (and the F-Droid build, `scripts/build-fdroid.sh`)\n   and confirm that `androidx.swiperefreshlayout:swiperefreshlayout:1.1.0`\n   resolves and the three Java files compile.\n2. Work through the TASK-5 checklist in `implementation.md` on Android <15\n   and 15+, in light and dark mode:\n   - pulling at the top reloads\n   - scrolling a long list back up does not reload\n   - no reload inside a modal, bottom sheet, kanban drag or calendar drag\n   - the spinner shows below the status bar and the WebView's edge-to-edge\n     margins are still correct\n   - the share intent still opens `/share`\n\n   Record the results in `implementation.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":24,"newStart":1,"newLines":91,"lines":[" # Verdict: Swipe from top to reload"," "," id: object","-reviewer:","-date:","+reviewer: @reviewer","+date: 2026-10-14"," ","-<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->","-"," ## Review"," ","-<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL","-     notes: ...","+Branch checked: `feature/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload` (matches brief).","+Base: `main` (`.manigot/manigot.json` is missing, so I used the default).","+I reviewed the whole `git diff main...HEAD`. Every source change is in `android/`;","+`frontend/` was not touched, as the plan required."," ","-TASK-2: ...","--->","+I could not compile anything either: there is no JDK, Gradle, Android SDK or","+`node_modules/@capacitor` here. So the Java was checked by reading only, against","+the Capacitor 7.6.8 sources the developer quoted in `session.log`","+(`CapacitorWebView.edgeToEdgeHandler`, `WebViewListener`, `BridgeActivity`)."