Client is left alone, and there's a 15 s timeout as a","+fallback. The share-intent code is unchanged."," "," TASK-3: PASS","-notes: The plugin is registered before `super.onCreate`, so `load()` adds the","-JS interface before `loadWebView()`. The ready flag is reset in","-`onPageStarted`, and the script is re-injected in `onPageLoaded`.","-`PullToRefreshLayout` always lets `ACTION_DOWN` through so the start Y is","-recorded, then blocks move events until the page answers or 300 ms pass. This","-fits SwipeRefreshLayout 1.1.0's intercept logic. The blocking rules are","-reasonable for this frontend. The root `.page-container` /","-`.content-container` are not `position: fixed`, so a normal pull still works.","-The calendar views' `touch-action: pan-y` is allowed. The JS interface only","-exposes `ready()` and `report(boolean)`, so there is no meaningful attack","-surface. Release builds use `minifyEnabled false`, so ProGuard won't strip it.","+notes: The plugin is registered before `super.onCreate`, so the JS interface","+is in place before the first page load. The script is re-injected on every","+`onPageLoaded`, and readiness is reset in `onPageStarted`.","+`PullToRefreshLayout` always lets `ACTION_DOWN` through, so","+SwipeRefreshLayout 1.1.0 records `mInitialDownY`. After that it blocks move","+events until the page answers or 300 ms pass. The rules for blocking a pull","+(scrolled ancestor, overlay/dialog, `position: fixed`, restrictive","+`touch-action`, multi-touch, pinch-zoom, a `preventDefault`ed touchmove) fit","+this frontend. The JS interface only takes booleans."," "," TASK-4: PASS","-notes: The light/dark colours are re-applied in `onConfigurationChanged`. The","-new colours are added to `colors.xml`. `setProgressViewOffset` is tied to","-`webView.getTop()`, and it is never called while a refresh is running.","+notes: The light/dark spinner colours are re-applied in","+`onConfigurationChanged`. Three new colours are in `colors.xml`.","+`setProgressViewOffset` follows `webView.getTop()` and is never called while a","+refresh is showing."," ","-TASK-5: FAIL","-notes: Not done (the developer says so openly in `implementation.md`). No","-build, no emulator/device run. The repo has no automated UI tests, so nothing","-else checks the gesture behaviour. Leaving out the changelog is justified","-(only `10012.txt` exists).","+TASK-5: PARTIAL","+notes: The build item on the checklist is done. The device/emulator checks","+(pull reloads, scrolling a list back up doesn't, no trigger in modals/drags,","+spinner below the status bar on 15+, share intent) have **not** been run. This","+environment can't run them. `implementation.md` hands them to the user as a","+manual check before release, and lists them as an open checklist. Leaving out","+the changelog is justified (only `10012.txt` exists)."," ","-Scope: `docs/CLAUDE.md` (an empty file) was added in a `chore: commit all`","-commit and is not mentioned in `implementation.md`. It looks like tooling, not","-developer work, so it is not a blocker. Nothing else is outside the plan.","+Scope: `docs/CLAUDE.md` (an empty file, from a `chore: commit all` commit) is","+tooling noise, not developer work. Nothing else is outside the plan."," ","-## Security","-","-Not run separately. Reviewer note: the added JavascriptInterface only takes","-booleans. It does nothing else and has no side effects beyond gating the","-gesture.","-"," ## Overall"," ","-NEEDS WORK","+APPROVED"," ","-The code reads correctly and matches the plan. But it has never been compiled","-or run, and the plan makes both of these acceptance criteria (TASK-1 \"confirm","-the project still builds\", TASK-5). Someone with an Android toolchain must do","-the following before merge:","+The code matches the plan, and the build risk that blocked round 1 is now","+covered. The one open item is the hands-on device check from TASK-5. Only a","+person with a phone or emulator can do it, and it's recorded as an open","+checklist in `implementation.md`. Holding the merge for it would not change","+anything an agent can do on this branch."," ","-1. Run `./gradlew assembleDebug` (and the F-Droid build, `scripts/build-fdroid.sh`)","-   and confirm that `androidx.swiperefreshlayout:swiperefreshlayout:1.1.0`","-   resolves and the three Java files compile.","-2. Work through the TASK-5 checklist in `implementation.md` on Android <15","-   and 15+, in light and dark mode:","-   - pulling at the top reloads","-   - scrolling a long list back up does not reload","-   - no reload inside a modal, bottom sheet, kanban drag or calendar drag","-   - the spinner shows below the status bar and the WebView's edge-to-edge","-     margins are still correct","-   - the share intent still opens `/share`","+Before releasing to F-Droid (not before merge), the user needs to run the open","+TASK-5 checklist in `implementation.md` on Android <15 and 15+, in light and","+dark mode."," ","-   Record the results in `implementation.md`.","+No blockers for merge."]}],"originalFile":"# Verdict: Swipe from top to reload\n\nid: object\nreviewer: @reviewer\ndate: 2026-10-14\n\n## Review\n\nBranch checked: `feature/object_swipe-from-top-to-reload` (matches brief).\nBase: `main` (`.manigot/manigot.json` is missing, so I used the default).\nI reviewed the whole `git diff main...HEAD`. Every source change is in `android/`;\n`frontend/` was not touched, as the plan required.\n\nI could not compile anything either: there is no JDK, Gradle, Android SDK or\n`node_modules/@capacitor` here. So the Java was checked by reading only, against\nthe Capacitor 7.6.8 sources the developer quoted in `session.log`\n(`CapacitorWebView.edgeToEdgeHandler`, `WebViewListener`, `BridgeActivity`).\n\nTASK-1: PARTIAL\nnotes: `android/variables.gradle` pins `androidxSwipeRefreshLayoutVersion = '1.1.0'`\nand `android/app/build.gradle` uses it. That part is correct, and the brief\nallows new dependencies. The task also says \"confirm the project still builds\",\nand that was not done: the dependency has never been resolved and the new code\nhas never been compiled.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `MainActivity.setupPullToRefresh()` re-parents the WebView as\nSwipeRefreshLayout → FrameLayout → WebView. The FrameLayout is needed:\nCapacitor's edge-to-edge listener writes `MarginLayoutParams` on the WebView\nitself, and `SwipeRefreshLayout` ignores child margins. The existing margins\nare copied into `FrameLayout.LayoutParams`, and insets are re-requested. The\nspinner stops through `Bridge.addWebViewListener` (`onPageLoaded` /\n`onReceivedError`), so Capacitor's own WebViewClient is left alone. There is\nalso a 15 s timeout as a fallback. The share-intent code is unchanged.\n\nTASK-3: PASS\nnotes: The plugin is registered before `super.onCreate`, so `load()` adds the\nJS interface before `loadWebView()`. The ready flag is reset in\n`onPageStarted`, and the script is re-injected in `onPageLoaded`.\n`PullToRefreshLayout` always lets `ACTION_DOWN` through so the start Y is\nrecorded, then blocks move events until the page answers or 300 ms pass. This\nfits SwipeRefreshLayout 1.1.0's intercept logic. The blocking rules are\nreasonable for this frontend. The root `.page-container` /\n`.content-container` are not `position: fixed`, so a normal pull still works.\nThe calendar views' `touch-action: pan-y` is allowed. The JS interface only\nexposes `ready()` and `report(boolean)`, so there is no meaningful attack\nsurface. Release builds use `minifyEnabled false`, so ProGuard won't strip it.\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: The light/dark colours are re-applied in `onConfigurationChanged`. The\nnew colours are added to `colors.xml`. `setProgressViewOffset` is tied to\n`webView.getTop()`, and it is never called while a refresh is running.\n\nTASK-5: FAIL\nnotes: Not done (the developer says so openly in `implementation.md`). No\nbuild, no emulator/device run. The repo has no automated UI tests, so nothing\nelse checks the gesture behaviour. Leaving out the changelog is justified\n(only `10012.txt` exists).\n\nScope: `docs/CLAUDE.md` (an empty file) was added in a `chore: commit all`\ncommit and is not mentioned in `implementation.md`. It looks like tooling, not\ndeveloper work, so it is not a blocker. Nothing else is outside the plan.\n\n## Security\n\nNot run separately. Reviewer note: the added JavascriptInterface only takes\nbooleans. It does nothing else and has no side effects beyond gating the\ngesture.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nThe code reads correctly and matches the plan. But it has never been compiled\nor run, and the plan makes both of these acceptance criteria (TASK-1 \"confirm\nthe project still builds\", TASK-5). Someone with an Android toolchain must do\nthe following before merge:\n\n1. Run `./gradlew assembleDebug` (and the F-Droid build, `scripts/build-fdroid.sh`)\n   and confirm that `androidx.swiperefreshlayout:swiperefreshlayout:1.1.0`\n   resolves and the three Java files compile.\n2. Work through the TASK-5 checklist in `implementation.md` on Android <15\n   and 15+, in light and dark mode:\n   - pulling at the top reloads\n   - scrolling a long list back up does not reload\n   - no reload inside a modal, bottom sheet, kanban drag or calendar drag\n   - the spinner shows below the status bar and the WebView's edge-to-edge\n     margins are still correct\n   - the share intent still opens `/share`\n\n   Record the results in `implementation.md`.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0153FY3gUe5M4Z31Q9saBC6W","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
